Hello everyone,<br><br>today bullet-physics-playground made it onto the news page of the raytracing application POV-Ray <a href="http://povray.org/" class="postlink">http://povray.org/</a>.<br><br>During the last three months a few new still images and animations were created.<br><br>Long term POV-Ray user Jaime Vives Piqueres <a href="http://www.ignorancia.org/" class="postlink">http://www.ignorancia.org/</a> created some nice arrangements of which my 3 favourites are:<br><div class="inline-attachment"><dl class="file"><dt class="attach-image"><img src="https://pybullet.org/Bullet/phpBB3/download/file.php?id=1006" class="postimage" alt="Alphabet blocks 02 by Jaime Vives Piqueres 2012." onclick="viewableArea(this);" /></dt></dl></div><div class="inline-attachment"><dl class="file"><dt class="attach-image"><img src="https://pybullet.org/Bullet/phpBB3/download/file.php?id=1005" class="postimage" alt="Pills many 07 by Jaime Vives Piqueres 2012." onclick="viewableArea(this);" /></dt></dl></div><div class="inline-attachment"><dl class="file"><dt class="attach-image"><img src="https://pybullet.org/Bullet/phpBB3/download/file.php?id=1004" class="postimage" alt="POV keyring 05 by Jaime Vives Piqueres 2012." onclick="viewableArea(this);" /></dt></dl></div>A lot of more still images and a few new animations can be found on the G+ community:<br><br>  <a href="https://plus.google.com/communities/118046861018657351607" class="postlink">https://plus.google.com/communities/118 ... 8657351607</a><br><br><br>Jakob<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="https://pybullet.org/Bullet/phpBB3/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=5661">koppi</a> — Thu Dec 06, 2012 8:10 pm</p><hr />
]]></content>
