		<content type="html" xml:base="https://pybullet.org/Bullet/phpBB3/viewtopic.php?p=28714#p28714"><![CDATA[
Hello everyone,<br><br>currently, we're building a team around <a href="https://github.com/koppi/bullet-physics-playground" class="postlink">https://github.com/koppi/bullet-physics-playground</a>.<br><br>The project still has some sort of HelloWorld status:<br><br>Currently it features Bullet, OpenGL, LUA scripting and POV-Ray export (-- YouTube needs more POV anims <img class="smilies" src="https://pybullet.org/Bullet/phpBB3/images/smilies/icon_wink.gif" width="15" height="15" alt=":wink:" title="Wink"> ).<br><br>We recently added <strong class="text-strong">build instructions</strong> for <strong class="text-strong">Windows</strong> and <strong class="text-strong">Linux</strong>:<br><ul><li> <a href="https://github.com/koppi/bullet-physics-playground/wiki/Build-on-Windows" class="postlink">https://github.com/koppi/bullet-physics ... on-Windows</a></li><li> <a href="https://github.com/koppi/bullet-physics-playground/wiki/Build-on-Linux" class="postlink">https://github.com/koppi/bullet-physics ... d-on-Linux</a></li></ul>If you want to get started with the bullet physics library and lua scripting, this is your time to jump in.<br><br>I will be accepting all your pull requests, so feel free to fork, patch, build and toy in your own physics world.<br><br>Jakob<br><br>P.S.: please note - will be offline for the next three months (no internet) and won't respond to any mails until 2012/12/12.<dl class="file"><dt class="attach-image"><img src="https://pybullet.org/Bullet/phpBB3/download/file.php?id=975" class="postimage" alt="lego car koppi" onclick="viewableArea(this);" /></dt></dl><p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="https://pybullet.org/Bullet/phpBB3/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=5661">koppi</a> — Sun Sep 09, 2012 3:08 pm</p><hr />
]]></content>
